content.text:
The telemetry points to one fault: ts-preserve-service, as an HTTP abort on its outgoing POST to ts-travel-service. Every other shift I checked is a traffic-mix effect or benign.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-preserve-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_aborted",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT cl.attr_status_code cl_status, sv.service_name sv_svc, sv.attr_status_code sv_status, sv.attr_http_response_status_code sv_code, count(*) n, round(avg(cl.duration)/1e6,1) cl_ms, round(avg(sv.duration)/1e6,1) sv_ms FROM abnormal_traces cl LEFT JOIN abnormal_traces sv ON sv.parent_span_id = cl.span_id AND sv.trace_id = cl.trace_id AND sv.attr_span_kind='Server' WHERE cl.service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND cl.attr_span_kind='Client' AND cl.span_name='POST' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "All 242 preserve POST calls to travel error with no HTTP status, while travel's server replies 200 in about 255 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, count(*) n, any_value(message) ex FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level NOT IN ('INFO','DEBUG','info','debug') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "ts-preserve-service logs 241 SEVERE 'Unexpected end of file from server' errors on POST to ts-travel-service trip_detail."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Preserve's POST /preserve server spans fail with 500 (242 of 242) in the incident window; normal period had 0 errors."
        },
